# Icons, states & loading

> Purpose: locked icon system, shared state screens, skeletons, lazy load. Never skipped or replaced with one-offs.

## Icon system

One primary system per project. If the installer names one, that choice wins. If they leave it blank, the AI picks one during **install** and writes the key into Profile **Icons** and `frontend-design/SKILL.md`. After install, use that key. Do not recommend again, and do not leave Icons as `TBD`.

| Key | System | Fits when |
|-----|--------|-----------|
| `material` | **Material Icons** / Material Symbols | Cross-platform web, Android-style UI, admin, dashboards. Default recommendation when nothing else fits better |
| `fontawesome` | **Font Awesome** (one style: solid or regular) | A wide classic set for marketing and app chrome; official package or SVG, not a copied webfont from elsewhere |
| `flaticon` | **Flaticon** SVGs in the repo | The concept needs a broader flat/illustrated set. Licensed pack only; no hotlink to flaticon.com; keep attribution if that license requires it |
| `sf-symbols` | **SF Symbols** (Apple) | The product surface is Apple-native (iOS, iPadOS, macOS). Not the chrome set for web or Android |
| `lottie` | **Lottie** JSON (`.json` / `.lottie`) | Brand or state moments need motion (404, empty, success). Official player; assets under `public/lottie/` or `src/assets/lottie/`; lightweight loops |

Recommend in the design REC: one Recommended key and why it fits **this** concept (surface, tone, motion), plus one alternative and its trade-off.

Rules:

- One static set for chrome. Emoji is not product chrome
- `lottie` may animate state screens over the static set; write that hybrid in Profile. Do not mix two static sets (Material + Font Awesome + Flaticon)
- `sf-symbols` stays on Apple surfaces. A `web` or `web + mobile` project that includes a browser uses `material`, `fontawesome`, or `flaticon` for shared chrome
- Icon-only controls still need accessible names (`aria-label` / visible text)
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`: pause Lottie, and do not rely on motion-only SF Symbol effects

## Default state screens (required)

Ship shared, reusable screens/components — not ad-hoc per page:

| State | Required |
|-------|----------|
| **404** Not found | Animated/illustrated default page (route catch-all) |
| **Other status errors** | Shared error page/panel for 403, 500, offline, generic failure (status + message + recovery CTA when useful) |
| **Empty data** | Shared empty state for lists/tables/search with optional action |

Prefer Lottie (or the chosen icon system) for these animations so they match brand motion. Copy and CTAs follow project tokens — not bare browser defaults.

## Skeleton loaders (required)

- List, detail, dashboard, and other async content regions use **skeleton loaders** while loading
- Skeletons match layout shape (not a lone spinner unless the surface is tiny)
- Shared skeleton primitives in `components/ui/` (or equivalent)

## Which loader (pick one)

Use the shared components in `reference/components/actions.md`. One loader per moment — do not stack a spinner on top of a skeleton.

| Moment | Use | Not this |
|--------|-----|----------|
| First load of a page, list, detail, dashboard, or chart | **Skeleton** shaped like the final layout | Full-screen spinner or blank page |
| Next page of a long list | **Infinite scroll** — sentinel + skeleton rows at the foot (`lists.md`) | Replacing the whole list with a skeleton |
| Button submit or save | **Button loader** — inline spinner, width locked, no second submit | A spinner beside the button |
| Route change, data still pending after ~150ms | **Top progress bar** (indeterminate) | Freezing the screen |
| Upload, export, or import when the percent is known | **Progress bar** with label | A skeleton or a fake percent |
| App or PWA boot, under 1.5s | **Splash** (`app-system.md`) | A long preloader on every visit |
| Tiny inline wait (icon, chip, refresh) | **Spinner** | A skeleton |
| Rare blocking step (payment confirm) | **Overlay loader** | Overlay on ordinary fetches |

**Default:** skeleton for content, button loader for actions, top bar for navigation, progress bar only when the amount done is known.

## Lazy load (required)

- Route-level **lazy loading** for feature screens/chunks
- Lazy-load heavy media / below-fold images where the stack supports it
- Lottie players and large animations load on demand when practical (do not block first paint)

## Do not

- Replace skeletons with blank screens or only spinners for primary content
- Eager-load every route/chunk when lazy load is available
- Swap the icon system mid-project without updating Profile + skill
- Mix two static icon sets for the same chrome layer (`lottie` may animate states over the chosen static set — note the hybrid in Profile)
- Use SF Symbols on the web, or hotlink Flaticon assets
